\section*{Symmetry of bounded semialgebraic domains with compact quotient}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
With cocompact biholomorphisms, a connected semialgebraic bounded open set in a complex affine variety is claimed to be smooth and biholomorphically equivalent to a symmetric domain that is bounded. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} Let $U$ be a nonempty connected bounded semialgebraic open subset of a complex affine variety in a fixed closed embedding into $\mathbb C^N$. Suppose a biholomorphism group $\Gamma$ acts properly discontinuously and $U/\Gamma$ is compact. OpenAI claims
\[
U\text{ is smooth and biholomorphic to a bounded symmetric domain}.
\]
A bounded symmetric domain is one in which each point is isolated in the fixed locus of a holomorphic involution. Initial smoothness, freeness of the action, and algebraicity of the biholomorphisms are not assumed.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 058, 2026-09-24): Holomorphic supports and analytic discs select a noncollapsing boundary model despite possible ambient singularities. Joint normal-offset limits and weighted dilation give a quadratic domain; convergence of both maps and inverses identifies the original domain with it, and the homogeneous-domain theorem supplies symmetry.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 058, 2026-09-24): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 058, the scope page documents the following selections. The selected bounded-domain result allows a singular affine ambient set and nonfree proper cocompact group action, and concludes smoothness and symmetry. It does not select the entire projective universal-cover classification. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Comparator files: SymmetricDomains.lean. Declarations: OAI.Release061.main.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

